A pizza with a diameter of 15 inches is cut into equal slices, each with a central angle of \(36^{\circ}\). Determine the length of the crust on the outer edge of one slice of pizza.

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{array}{rlr}
\frac{36^{\circ}}{180^{\circ}} & =\frac{\theta}{\pi} & \\
\theta & =\frac{\pi}{5} & 1 \text { mark for conversion } \\
s & =\theta r & \\
s & =\left(\frac{\pi}{5}\right)\left(\frac{15}{2}\right) & 1 \text { mark for substitution } \\
s & =\frac{3 \pi}{2} \text { inches } & 2 \text { marks } \\
\text { or } & & \\
s & =4.712 \text { inches }
\end{array}
\]

